        <div class=3D"card-subtitle">Investment Thesis</div>
      </div>
      <p class=3D"body">Intertek Group plc is a global leader in Testing, I=
nspection &amp; Certification (TIC) services, operating across 100+ countri=
es with a highly defensible business model built on regulatory mandates, mi=
ssion-critical quality assurance workflows, and exceptionally high switchin=
g costs. The company serves a diverse range of end markets including consum=
er products, chemicals, energy, and business assurance.</p>
      <p class=3D"body">Our analysis indicates that Intertek is modestly un=
dervalued relative to its intrinsic worth, and represents a compelling stra=
tegic acquisition candidate for a diversified industrials conglomerate or a=
 large-scale PE buyout. The company's asset-light model, strong free cash f=
low conversion (&gt;85%), and organic growth engine make it an attractive L=
BO or bolt-on platform candidate.</p>
      <div class=3D"highlight-box">
        <strong>Key Finding:</strong> DCF-derived intrinsic value of <stron=
g>3,840p per share</strong> implies 15.7% upside to the current market pric=
e of ~3,320p. Under a transaction scenario at sector precedent multiples (1=
5=E2=80=9317=C3=97 EBITDA), equity value per share would reach <strong>4,25=
0=E2=80=934,800p</strong>, representing 28=E2=80=9345% premium to the undis=
turbed share price.
      </div>
    </div>

