<div class=3D"section active" id=3D"p1">
  <div class=3D"section-badge">Part I</div>
  <div class=3D"section-header">Company Overview</div>
  <div class=3D"section-desc">Business model, products, competitive positio=
ning, and investment highlights for Intertek Group plc.</div>

  <div class=3D"grid-2">
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"card-header">
        <div class=3D"card-title">Business Model</div>
        <div class=3D"card-subtitle">Total Quality Assurance</div>
      </div>
      <p class=3D"body">Intertek operates as a <strong>testing, inspection,=
 and certification (TIC)</strong> provider under its Total Quality Assuranc=
e (TQA) framework. The company earns revenue by conducting product testing,=
 auditing supply chains, certifying compliance with safety and regulatory s=
tandards, and inspecting infrastructure and industrial assets across global=
 operations.</p>
      <p class=3D"body">Revenue is <strong>highly recurring and regulatory-=
driven</strong>: clients are often legally required to certify products, ob=
tain safety marks (CE, UL, REACH), or maintain inspection regimes. This cre=
ates sticky, mission-critical demand with high switching costs =E2=80=94 ch=
anging a TIC provider mid-certification cycle is operationally disruptive a=
nd reputationally risky.</p>
      <div class=3D"navy-box">
        <strong>Revenue Recognition:</strong> Services are charged on a per=
-test, per-project, or retainer basis. ~60% of revenues are recurring or se=
mi-recurring in nature. CapEx intensity is low (~3=E2=80=934% of revenue), =
as value creation is driven by human capital (chemists, engineers, auditors=
) and accredited laboratory assets.
      </div>
      <h4>Four Reporting Divisions</h4>
      <table class=3D"data-table" style=3D"margin-top:0.5rem;">
        <thead><tr><th>Division</th><th>Revenue Share</th><th>EBIT Margin</=
th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Products (Consumer &amp; Retail)</td><td>38%</td><td>18=
=E2=80=9320%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Trade (Commodities &amp; Trade Finance)</td><td>20%</td><=
td>14=E2=80=9316%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Resources (Energy &amp; Industrials)</td><td>22%</td><td>=
16=E2=80=9318%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Industry &amp; Assurance (B2B)</td><td>20%</td><td>17=E2=
=80=9319%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"card-header">
        <div class=3D"card-title">Competitive Positioning</div>
        <div class=3D"card-subtitle">Market Leadership</div>
      </div>
      <h5>Market Position</h5>
      <p class=3D"body">Intertek is the <strong>#3 global TIC player</stron=
g> by revenue behind SGS (Switzerland) and Bureau Veritas (France), but wit=
h superior margins and stronger organic growth. Combined, the top 4 players=
 (SGS, Bureau Veritas, Intertek, Eurofins) control ~25% of the highly fragm=
ented ~=C2=A3200bn global TIC market.</p>
      <h4>Key Competitive Advantages</h4>
      <ul class=3D"bullets">
        <li><strong>Accreditation network</strong> =E2=80=94 1,000+ accredi=
tations globally. These take years and significant CapEx to replicate, crea=
ting a structural barrier to entry.</li>
        <li><strong>Global footprint</strong> =E2=80=94 100+ countries, 43,=
000+ employees. Clients with global supply chains require a single TIC part=
ner, benefiting scale players.</li>
        <li><strong>Brand / Trust</strong> =E2=80=94 Intertek's ATIC mark i=
s internationally recognised. Brand trust is existential in certification =
=E2=80=94 clients cannot risk a substandard provider.</li>
        <li><strong>ATIC Framework</strong> =E2=80=94 Proprietary Total Qua=
lity Assurance methodology enabling cross-sell and wallet share expansion w=
ithin existing clients.</li>
        <li><strong>Regulatory tailwind</strong> =E2=80=94 EU Green Deal, C=
SRD, product safety directives, and ESG reporting mandates structurally exp=
and the addressable market.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>Market Size (TAM)</h4>
      <div class=3D"progress-bar-wrap" style=3D"margin-bottom:4px;"><div cl=
ass=3D"progress-bar-fill" style=3D"width:100%;"></div></div>
      <div style=3D"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);">Total TIC Mark=
et: ~=C2=A3200bn globally, ~=C2=A345bn addressable for Intertek's specific =
services</div>
      <div class=3D"grid-2" style=3D"margin-top:1rem; gap:0.75rem;">
        <div class=3D"metric-tile gold"><div class=3D"metric-label">Global =
TIC TAM</div><div class=3D"metric-value">=C2=A3200bn</div><div class=3D"met=
ric-sub">~5% annual growth</div></div>
        <div class=3D"metric-tile gold"><div class=3D"metric-label">Interte=
k Market Share</div><div class=3D"metric-value">~1.5%</div><div class=3D"me=
tric-sub">Significant runway</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"card">
    <div class=3D"card-header"><div class=3D"card-title">Investment Highlig=
hts</div><div class=3D"card-subtitle">Why This Business Commands Premium Mu=
ltiples</div></div>
    <div class=3D"grid-3">
      <div>
        <h4>=F0=9F=94=92 Regulatory Moat</h4>
        <p class=3D"body" style=3D"font-size:12px;">Regulatory compliance m=
andates (CE marking, REACH, FDA, OSHA) create non-discretionary demand. Cli=
ents are legally required to certify products =E2=80=94 Intertek's services=
 are embedded into supply chain workflows.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>=F0=9F=92=B0 Asset-Light FCF Engine</h4>
        <p class=3D"body" style=3D"font-size:12px;">CapEx/Revenue ~3.5%. FC=
F conversion &gt;85%. ROIC of 22.4% significantly exceeds the WACC of 8.5%,=
 creating substantial economic value. Dividend payer with progressive polic=
y.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>=F0=9F=8C=8D Geographic Diversification</h4>
        <p class=3D"body" style=3D"font-size:12px;">Americas (35%), EMEA (3=
0%), Asia Pacific (35%). No single market &gt;20% of revenue. Exposure to e=
merging market growth (Southeast Asia, South America) with developed market=
 stability.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>=F0=9F=93=88 Structural Growth Tailwinds</h4>
        <p class=3D"body" style=3D"font-size:12px;">ESG, sustainability rep=
orting (CSRD), supply chain transparency, battery/EV testing, food safety, =
cybersecurity certifications =E2=80=94 all represent new, growing demand se=
gments for TIC services.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>=F0=9F=94=84 M&amp;A Platform</h4>
        <p class=3D"body" style=3D"font-size:12px;">TIC is highly fragmente=
d with thousands of small regional players. Intertek has a disciplined bolt=
-on M&amp;A strategy with 10-15+ acquisitions in recent history, all integr=
ating at attractive ROIC.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>=F0=9F=8E=AF Strategic Premium Candidate</h4>
        <p class=3D"body" style=3D"font-size:12px;">Acquirable at =C2=A35=
=E2=80=937bn by a diversified industrial conglomerate (Danaher, Fortive) or=
 PE consortium. Network synergies with SGS or Bureau Veritas would be trans=
formational =E2=80=94 regulators permitting.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D PART 2 =
