    <div class=3D"grid-2">
      <div>
        <h4>Revenue Trajectory</h4>
        <p class=3D"body">Organic revenue growth averaged 5.7% CAGR over 20=
20=E2=80=932024E, comfortably above UK GDP growth and in line with broader =
TIC sector rates. The 2023 slowdown to +1.7% reflects: (1) normalisation po=
st-Covid-era supply chain disruption boom; (2) macro softness in industrial=
 segments; and (3) FX headwinds from sterling appreciation. The 2024 recove=
ry to +5.2% organic is driven by continued ESG-related testing demand and n=
ew lab capacity in Asia Pacific.</p>
        <h4>Margin Evolution</h4>
        <p class=3D"body">EBITDA margins have held in a narrow 18.8=E2=80=
=9319.2% band, demonstrating the business's operational resilience. The fla=
t-to-improving margin trajectory masks strong underlying operating leverage=
: revenue has grown at ~6% while headcount growth has been contained to ~3=
=E2=80=934% via increased automation and offshore laboratory operations.</p=
>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Capital Intensity</h4>
        <p class=3D"body">Intertek is characteristically asset-light for an=
 industrials-adjacent business. CapEx has held at ~3.5% of revenues =E2=80=
=94 well below sector peers in contract testing (6=E2=80=938%) and far belo=
w asset-heavy comparables. This drives structurally superior FCF conversion=
 and ROIC. The primary CapEx driver is laboratory equipment investment and =
geographic expansion.</p>
        <h4>Cash Generation Quality</h4>
        <p class=3D"body">FCF conversion of ~70% of EBITDA (improving to ~7=
2% in 2024E) is exceptional for an industrials company. Net debt has declin=
ed consistently from 2.1=C3=97 EBITDA in 2020 to 1.6=C3=97 in 2024E despite=
 a progressive dividend policy and bolt-on M&amp;A. The balance sheet suppo=
rts acquisition capacity of =C2=A31.5=E2=80=932.0bn without a rights issue,=
 making Intertek itself a credible buyer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"highlight-box">
      <strong>Institutional Commentary:</strong> Intertek's financial profi=
le closely mirrors enterprise software companies in terms of revenue qualit=
y (recurring, sticky), margin structure (high and stable), and capital effi=
ciency (ROIC significantly above WACC). This justifies a premium multiple v=
ersus traditional industrials, but the current 11.8=C3=97 EV/EBITDA implies=
 a meaningful discount to software and to specialty services peers trading =
at 13=E2=80=9317=C3=97. The discount likely reflects perceived macro sensit=
ivity in trade/resources segments and Intertek's UK listing (discount vs. E=
uropean peers).
    </div>
