lisation, higher ERP</td></tr>
          <tr class=3D"highlight"><td>Base Case</td><td>8.5%</td><td>Curren=
t market conditions</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bull (Lower)</td><td>7.5%</td><td>Rate cuts, lower ERP en=
vironment</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class=3D"highlight-box" style=3D"margin-top:1rem;">
        <strong>Beta Justification:</strong> Intertek's beta of 0.82 reflec=
ts its quasi-defensive characteristics (regulatory demand floor) with modes=
t cyclical exposure (trade/resources). This is consistent with sector peers=
 (SGS 0.78, BV 0.79, Eurofins 0.84). The beta is measurably below the broad=
er FTSE 100 market beta of 1.0, reflecting the annuity-like nature of TIC r=
evenues.
      </div>
